Grouped MoE expert mat-vec for SYCL prefill (on top of llama.cpp-moe-hot-cold-experts.patch and
llama.cpp-moe-dynamic-residency.patch; same base). Measurements: docs/INTEL_ONLY_MOE.md, "Prefill: grouped MUL_MAT_ID".

- MUL_MAT_ID with many tokens: the routed rows, already sorted by expert, are quantized to Q8_1 once and cut into
  tiles of at most 8 rows of one expert; one kernel launch covers every tile of every expert. A subgroup reads one
  weight row once per tile and applies it to all of the tile's rows. This replaces "dequantize the whole expert to f16,
  then GEMM" per expert, which costs ~190 us per expert at these shapes however few rows the expert receives.
- IQ2_XXS / IQ2_S / IQ3_XXS: decode-once kernel - a lane decodes its 32 codebook weights once into signed int8x4
  words, then 8 dp4a per row (the generic vec_dot re-decodes per token; IQ2_XXS's is scalar).
- Hybrid per expert: experts with <= 48 rows (decode-once types; 14 / 8 rows for the generic kernel) use the grouped
  launch, larger ones keep the GEMM path. Decode (one token) is unchanged.
- GGML_SYCL_MMID_GROUPED=0 (off) / 1 (generic grouped) / 2 (default: + decode-once), GGML_SYCL_MMID_GROUPED_MAX_ROWS=N.
- test-backend-ops: perf cases at the GLM-5.3-Flash / DeepSeek V4 Flash expert shapes (4096 x 2048, 288 x top-8,
  256 x top-6).

